In this section, we present a formal, symbolic description of our feature localization algorithm. Specifically, given a target concept c c to be erased, we categorize it into two types: attribute-like concepts c a c_{a} (e.g., Nudity , VanGogh style ) and object-like concepts c o c_{o} (e.g., Church , Parachute ). For attribute-like concepts c a c_{a} , let 𝒟 c a \mathcal{D}_{c_{a}} be a dataset of prompts that contain c a c_{a} and 𝒟 ¬ c a \mathcal{D}_{
eg c_{a}} a paired dataset of prompts that do not contain c a c_{a} . For object-like concepts c o c_{o} , let 𝒟 c o \mathcal{D}_{c_{o}} be a dataset of prompts that containing c o c_{o} and 𝒟 ¬ c o \mathcal{D}_{
eg c_{o}} a dataset of prompts that exclude c o c_{o} but may include other objects; in this case, the two sets are not pairwise aligned. For convenience, we denote the dataset containing the target concept as 𝒟 c \mathcal{D}_{c} and the dataset excluding it as 𝒟 ¬ c \mathcal{D}_{
